PR Title: feat: Global App Reset Button

The Problem Solved: Users lacked a way to easily clear their entire session state (inputs, settings, generated audio, and progress) without reloading the page. This PR adds a one-click "Reset" button to the app header.

Visuals:
- [Screenshot: Global Reset Button](/home/jules/verification/screenshots/global-reset-button.png)

Implementation Journey:
- Branched to `feature/global-app-reset-button`.
- Evaluated multiple architectural approaches for a reset function (Full reload, Minimal icon, Standard state reset).
- Implemented `handleReset` in `web-ui/src/app/page.tsx` to cleanly clear all `useState` variables and abort ongoing operations.
- Added a `RotateCcw` button from `lucide-react` to the top-right of the header area using absolute positioning for a non-intrusive UI.
- Verified file changes locally and successfully ran the Next.js production build (`NEXT_DISABLE_ESLINT=1 npm run build` to respect the Surgical Changes protocol).
- Wrote and executed a Playwright script to verify the new UI component rendering.

Tradeoffs & Assumptions:
- **Assumption:** The user wanted a net-new feature to improve UX without complicating the core application logic.
- **Approach 1 (Lateral):** `window.location.reload()`. A poor SPA experience.
- **Approach 2 (Minimalist):** A small trash-can icon. Might be misinterpreted as "delete file".
- **Approach 3 (Standard):** A labeled reset button with a `RotateCcw` icon. Selected this route for maximum clarity and best React SPA practices by manually resetting state.
- **Tradeoff:** Using absolute positioning in the header instead of flex-wrap flow ensures the button does not disrupt the main layout on mobile, though it does slightly overlap the right edge of the header container boundary on very narrow screens.

Testing Instructions:
1. Start the dev server.
2. Upload a text or EPUB file, change a few settings (voice, speed).
3. Click "Start Generation".
4. While generating (or after), click the "Reset" button in the top right of the title header.
5. Verify that all inputs, settings, outputs, and statuses are cleared to default, and that the generation stops without errors.

